,"legacy":"banned","modern":"not_legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"banned","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"restricted"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{2}{U}","name":"Windfall","oracle_id":"08becc07-28bc-4a2f-a6b0-28a2998d2f50","oracle_text":"Each player discards their hand, then draws cards equal to the greatest number of cards a player discarded this way.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2024-04-19","toughness":null,"type_line":"Sorcery"}],"rulings":[{"comment":"If Rest in Peace is destroyed by a spell, Rest in Peace will be exiled and then the spell will be put into its owner's graveyard.","oracle_id":"087f9ad7-e74f-40e2-8102-1ed2925d0418","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a card is discarded while Rest in Peace is on the battlefield, abilities that function when a card is discarded (such as madness) still work, even though that card never reaches a graveyard. In addition, spells or abilities that check the characteristics of a discarded card (such as Chandra Ablaze's first ability) can find that card in exile.","oracle_id":"087f9ad7-e74f-40e2-8102-1ed2925d0418","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"While Rest in Peace is on the battlefield, abilities that trigger whenever a creature dies won't trigger because cards and tokens are never put into a player's graveyard.","oracle_id":"087f9ad7-e74f-40e2-8102-1ed2925d0418","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"It triggers only once even if blocked by more than one creature.","oracle_id":"0d44d4f3-9713-4d18-a985-9e7ff0df85d3","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"It counts how many cards you discard. Since this card will not be in your hand at that time, this card is not counted.","oracle_id":"686cce6e-18ec-45b0-8d2e-74fa353a905e","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The number of cards the player draws is equal to the number of cards they discarded, not the amount of damage dealt by Barbed Shocker.","oracle_id":"ae5cf0da-bea8-4ba7-9fb3-0fcb076257ae","published_at":"2006-09-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If some of the targets become illegal for Ral's second ability, the original division of damage still applies, and the damage that would have been dealt to illegal targets isn't dealt at all.","oracle_id":"d7b10518-b6dc-4a39-881a-edd346034f28","published_at":"2018-10-05","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
